  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Prashant Dhanpal Gandhi vs State Of Maharashtra on 9 May, 2024 Author: N.J.Jamadar Bench: N.J.Jamadar 2024:Bhc-As:22076 957 ba In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No.1670 Of 2024 Prashant Dhanpal Gandhi ... Applicant versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respond Mr. Prashant Subhash Hagare for Applicant. Mr. Tanveer Khan, App for State. Api Nagnath G. Patil, Supa Police Station present. Coram: N.J.Jamadar, J. Date : 9 May 2024 P.C. 1.",
    "facts": "2. The applicant who is arraigned in C.R.No.110 of 2024 registered Supa Police Station for the offences punishable under Section 328 and 188 of Indian Penal Code and Sections 27(2)(i), 3(1)(zz)(iv), 59, 26(2)(iv), 27(3)( (e) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, has preferred this applicati enlarge him on bail. 3. On 24 March 2024, pursuant to an intimation a raid was conducte the house of the applicant at Baramati. The applicant took the police party house at Udwandi, Supe, where contraband article - Gutkha was found kept in number of bags. Gutkha worth Rs.30,98,820/- was seized and the applicant was apprehended. Learned Counsel for the Applicant submitted that the applicabil SSP 1/3 957 ba 1670 of 2024.d provisions contained in Section 328 of IPC is debatable. Investigation is practically complete. Therefore, the applicant be released on bail. 5. Learned APP resisted the prayer for bail. It is submitted that the Applicant has been habitually indulging in procurement, transportation and sell of gutkha and a number of crimes have been registered against the applicant. Hence, the applicant does not deserve to be enlarged on bail.",
    "arguments": "",
